// Nothing pushes boxes apart, and a gap is exactly what was asked for.
//
// "middle" is placed between "left" and "right", so it is centered in the gap
// between them at its own size; neither of them moves to make room. Where a box
// lands on another, it is drawn there and the overlap is reported.

node left    "L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L/L"
node right   "R"                             right of left
node middle  "m"   right of left  left of right  even with left
node wide    "a wide box that overruns both"    below middle (gap: tight)
